  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1040 PM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nThe upper level low will slowly move north on Wednesday keeping\nscattered afternoon and early evening showers in the forecast for\nmainly the Plateau. CAPE will also start to tick up and a few \nthunderstorms will be possible during the afternoon. The upper \nlevel low will then phase into the flow later Wednesday into \nThursday as a trough digs into the Great Lakes and the Bermuda \nhigh pushes west some. Embedded short waves will spin around a \nstrong upper level ridge set up to our east for the second half of\nthe week into the weekend. This will keep scattered showers and \nthunderstorms in the forecast each day. By the end of the week we \nwill see quite a bit of CAPE in the afternoon but we will lack \nwind shear and overall forcing will be marginal. This will keep \nthe severe threat very low. Highs will be more seasonal by\nWednesday in the upper 80s to mid 90s and they will stay there\ninto the weekend.",
